1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:02:11,190
Part 3 is not on the source, so this part begins in the middle of Narada's talk. Either a person knowingly refuses the enjoyment of the senses, or the enjoyment never comes to him. The two have become one. One knowingly becomes an ascetic, leaves enjoyment, and goes to the forest. The pain of a poor man can match the austerity that others perform with great fondness and firmness. That pain itself is his austerity. He does not need a separate austerity. Other ascetics do practice austerity, but they have a pillar of ego, pride, arrogance. They do not bow before anyone. Intoxication comes. It is often heard that ascetics are very angry. By austerity, pride increases. It does not decrease. But a poor man who practices austerity has no pride left. If the austerity is already on him, where would pride come from? Such austerity is sound. It is beautiful. Austerity should be of this kind. Other ascetics have the pride, I have renounced so much, I have practiced austerity for so many days, I have stood so long.

2
00:02:11,190 --> 00:05:53,660
Like Durvasa. He went to Yudhishthira, and he came here to Mathura, to Maharaj Ambarisha. Ambarisha said, some of my duty is still unfinished, I am going to the Yamuna, please wait, do whatever you like. The time of Dvadashi began to pass. On the direction of his family priest and of those who knew scripture, Maharaj Ambarisha drank water, the water of the Lord's feet. Durvasa returned. By the power of yoga and by knowledge he understood that Ambarisha had eaten. He did not understand that it was done to complete the vow, and that it was not a meal. It was water. At that much, anger blazed. He tried to kill Ambarisha. He tore a hair from his locks and produced a witch. Kill him, burn him. If a meal is half an hour late, a sadhu can become this angry. Ambarisha had only drunk water. Seen in the ordinary way, the pride of austerity was so great that he was ready to take the life of so great a devotee. The misery that then came upon Durvasa is known to everyone. A poor man does not have the pride, I am suffering, I am practicing austerity. Among ascetics that pride comes. What does anyone have, that he can renounce it? I have given this up, I have given that up. Renunciation is only ego. No one has anything. Everything is the Lord's. Only the pride has to be given up. The feeling remains, this is mine. No one can wash it and take it away. After death it cannot be taken. While living it cannot be taken everywhere. Still, it is mine, it is mine. When a poor man is in pain, he does not think, I am a very fine ascetic. This is the distinction of the poor man's austerity.

3
00:05:55,420 --> 00:10:06,000
So Narada is saying, above, daridro niraham-stambhah. A stambha is a pillar, or a stump. One who will not bow before anyone. The pillar of I. I am something, I am like this. Even stambha alone would have been enough. Once, in a village near ours, two men were quarreling. One was a little rich, the other completely poor. The rich man said, what will you say to me? What your family spends in a whole year is spent on my medicine alone. On food, on cloth, on everything. What sort of praise is that? It means you are a very great patient. Pride is like this. I have had a bypass. They take off the cloth and show it. The body is cut further, and the pride increases. I went to Bangalore. This is the pillar. A story is told. In a king's house the queen fell ill, and the same day a servant fell ill. The royal physician examined them. The queen's fever was 101 degrees, the servant's 104 or 105. The moment the queen heard it, she was offended. What kind of physician is this? He gave me 101 and the servant 104. Do something so that my fever rises. I will not remain less than a servant. If fever comes, mine should be higher. If there is trouble, our trouble should be the great trouble. We are great people. If a tablet of fifty paise removes the fever, what name is there in that? When two or four lakh are spent, and there is a noise on every side, then it will be admitted that a great person was ill. If fever goes by drinking a decoction of tulasi, then what fever was it? This is the pillar of I. I am not a person whose illness is ordinary.

4
00:10:09,480 --> 00:16:54,180
Four intoxications are named. The intoxication of learning, of birth, of wealth, and of beauty. Beauty is not counted as a special one. Three are famous. Wealth, learning, and birth. I was born in such a great family. If something is to be spent, they seat many people and spend. We are great, we do not eat alone, we eat with ten or twenty. We will stay in a hotel that takes several thousand in a day. We cannot stay in an ordinary hotel. That is intoxication. But a poor man is freed from all these intoxications. There is no fault in him to begin with, and on top of that he has become an ascetic, so his austerity is very good. For him, that itself is the greatest austerity. One who is strong, his senses run toward their objects. The body is able to walk, to eat, to drink, to enjoy. What happens to the poor man? Every day his body is thin from hunger. Hunger is like a fire. If it is not given food, it begins to burn the body itself. The body becomes thin. The senses dry up. The strength of the senses lessens. Their running into the objects stops. This is a treatment. How the soul may be kept filled with Krishna consciousness, that remedy is being told. Even bread enough to fill the stomach does not come. A poor man desires only food. Give him food and he is satisfied. A rich man is not satisfied by food alone. Desire after desire remains. The poor man's other longings cannot remain. When he is hungry he will not think, I should travel by airplane. If food comes, that is enough. For a practitioner, to have no other desire in the heart is a great attainment. It is possible only through poverty. So, for devotion to grow, fasting is generally practiced. The rule has been that the mind should not be indulged. Eat whatever the mind fancies, then eat. Eat rubbish, like a goat, and keep eating. Petrol is not filled for the sake of the car. It is filled so that the car will run. If the car is running, there is no further need of petrol. A human being is such that he eats and drinks here and there. He leaves the house after eating, and then eats many dirty things. Someone is drinking. Someone begins to drink smoke. A poor man is freed from these faults. From hunger the body becomes thin, and the senses begin to dry.

5
00:16:56,220 --> 00:20:17,400
And violence also turns away. When the body is well and there is wealth, the tendency to give pain to others, by word and by body, goes away. Hell comes from violence. Nonviolence is the highest duty. By doing violence, by taking another's right, by killing, by giving pain, a person goes to hell. If he eats and drinks and gives pain to no one, there is no likelihood of hell. If pain has been given, hell is certain. If someone passed a rule that an ascetic, a poor man, a man without wealth, should be sent to hell because he has sinned, and that the enjoyers, the healthy, the rich, should be sent to heaven, he would have turned the rule upside down. To make every rule of Brahma's creation upside down was also Hiranyakashipu's purpose. He ordered the trees, give fruit all year. Do not give fruit for one month and then sit quiet. He ordered the earth, give a crop all year. He ordered the ocean, produce jewels twenty-four hours a day, all year. No rest, no holiday. People became miserable. Then there was prayer to the Lord. Let Lord Nrishimha come, kill him, change his rules, and apply His own. For all the enjoyers who enjoy by giving pain to others, a place in hell is already made. According to the Bhagavatam, if they live by giving pain, they will go to hell. If they have not given pain, they will not.

6
00:20:17,650 --> 00:24:04,920
A poor man receives one great benefit. Narada is telling it. The saints who see equally associate only with the poor. The Lord's devotees go to the poor man's house and meet the poor man. Those who see equally, in whose life there is no greed, who take the rich and the poor as the same, sit only with the poor. They do not go to the rich. Sri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu did not want to meet Maharaj Prataparudra. Many people said, please meet him, he is a great Vaishnava, he is attached to your feet, if you do not give him your sight he will die. The Lord knew everything. A king keeps all the opulence. If a sannyasi meets a king, the king will give him wealth, he will become an enjoyer, and the sannyasi will fall. So a rich man is a danger. A real devotee goes only to the poor. The poor man's nature is like theirs. Pride does not remain. The pillar of ego does not remain. He has time to hear the sadhu. Go to a rich man and he will say, sit in the reception room, I have no time, I am going to work. He will tell a servant, receive the sadhu. At most he will ask, what has he come for, he must have come for money, give it to him, I have no time. In the temple, those who think themselves low, who think themselves poor, sit at leisure in the line and eat the prasadam. The great people cannot sit. If they sit there, our lowness will be seen. That is the conviction in the mind. Narada is telling the principle. Sadhus meet the poor.

7
00:24:04,920 --> 00:27:48,080
Srimad-Bhagavatam is a spotless authority. When a poor man receives the company of a sadhu, he is very fertile ground. The seed of devotion can be placed there quickly. He is without ego and without these faults. After a little talk, after a little food, he becomes the Lord's devotee. By the saints, that thirst is weakened, and then he is quickly purified. By the sadhu's company, even his worldly thirst goes. Experiencing the happiness the sadhu is receiving, the thirst leaves. A rich man's thirst is hard to remove. It simply does not go. A poor man has thirst, but it has no support. By the sadhu's company it goes, and he is quickly purified. The mind catches hold of Krishna. It is like a child who has fallen asleep and will not wake to eat. The mother or the father wakes him. Sometimes he will not wake, he will not take the medicine, and the time has come. They hold the ear, press the hand, the nose, so that he will wake. Then they give the food. When the taste comes, he begins to eat. In the same way the Lord gives someone poverty. This is mercy. But the mercy is counted complete for those who, having become poor, also receive the company of a sadhu.

8
00:27:51,430 --> 00:31:44,090
By the company of sadhus, the thirst for sense enjoyment goes. When the thirst has gone, he is at once purified. The mind is fixed on the Lord. Therefore, tad aham mattayoh. As a father is merciful toward his two sons, so Narada Muni, having spoken this principle, speaks about Nalakuvara and Manigriva. Intoxicated and blinded by the fortune of varuni wine, I will take away the intoxication of their ignorance. As a very merciful physician, merciful to a patient seized by a great disease, says, I will remove his disease. They are capable. Like the Lord, what they wish to do, they can do. At this moment they are drunk on varuni wine. But one day I will make them drunk by giving them love of God. Now they are looking at the affairs of the world. One day they will see Krishna face to face. Narada has already considered this. They must be placed in a condition from which the sight of the Lord will come. This is compassion. He is saying aham, I. A sadhu never says, I will do this. Narada is saying it with a special feeling. If I have worshiped the Lord, then by the strength of that worship I will purify them. Here aham is not a word of blame.

9
00:31:47,600 --> 00:34:06,660
They are unconquered in themselves, lost in sporting with women. They are under the control of women and of the senses. I will remove the intoxication born of their ignorance. Every person's condition is the condition of Nalakuvara and Manigriva. A man who is advanced in the spiritual has one duty, to remove the intoxication of ignorance. The means of removing it is the Lord's katha, the preaching of the Lord. These two have sunk into ignorance. The body is a net of ignorance. They think the success of life is only to enjoy the enjoyments of the world. The intoxication has grown so far that they do not even know they are naked. Or they do not know that bathing naked is a mistake. Scripture allows some sense enjoyment, but it has a limit and a rule. If they begin to bathe and wander naked here and there, the limit of intoxication has been crossed. Narada is saying, their disease has become very great, and still I will remove the intoxication of ignorance. They do not know themselves. They do not even know that our father is Kuvera, we are this great, we should not act so low, we should not be so absorbed in enjoyment.

10
00:34:11,960 --> 00:39:14,460
Now these two are fit for the state of the immovable. Fit to enter the body of a tree. Sthavara means a tree. The poor things stay in one place. All their life they go nowhere. They do not wander. Where birth comes, there they remain. If they are uprooted and planted somewhere, they remain there for life. If they go anywhere, it is after death, as cut wood. So they are called immovable. The same demigods who were wandering on airplanes and sporting with women are now fit for the birth of the immovable. This is Narada's power. If he wishes, he can place someone in the body of a tree. So the words of the ancient acharyas and great souls should be taken as the ideal. Their conduct should not be copied. Narada said, let these two become trees, and they became trees. Leave aside a man today. Tell a dog, tell an insect, become a tree. It will not happen. Tell a mosquito, do not bite me. It will not obey. The people of former times were that capable. That is why he is called Bhagavan, devarshi. So that this will not happen again. So that such absorption in sense objects will not return. But even in the body of a tree, by the mercy of Vasudeva and by my favor, memory of the Lord will remain. Where is he giving them birth? In the circle of Braj, in Mahavana, in Gokula. The Lord's mercy follows the mercy of the sadhu. One devotee considered: these poor ones were sinning at Kailasa, in the Ganga, in a complete holy place, and they were naked, and still they received birth in Braj. There must have been some piety. Sridhara Swami says, whether they performed any auspicious work or not, I see one visible auspicious act. They were playing in the water of the Ganga. By the glory of the Ganga this opportunity came. They were playing in the water of the Lord's feet. The Ganga knows her own glory. They did not know it. They were absorbed in sense objects. Because of playing in the Ganga, they were not disregarded. In the birth of a tree, remembrance of Krishna, and Braj.

11
00:39:16,480 --> 00:43:39,200
Narada's wish is that they become the Lord's devotees, receive His mercy, and become His associates. Scripture calls this perfection by chance. Without practice, without auspicious work, a sadhu's mercy can fall on anyone. The Lord looks for practice. Vishvanatha Chakravarti Thakura says the Lord sees the practice. If practice has been done, He gives the destination. Even without practice the Lord gives an auspicious destination, when a sadhu directly wishes it. As a destination was given to the mother. But a sadhu's wish, a sadhu's mercy, can happen anywhere without practice. A sadhu's mercy is stronger than the Lord's mercy. The Lord's mercy follows behind the sadhu. Let this wish rise in the mind of a great sadhu. We are hearing the history of how two demigods received Narada's mercy and are being born in the circle of Braj. Even in an immovable body, a birth joined with full remembrance of Krishna. From the time they became trees, they stood in this Braj for a hundred celestial years, waiting for the Lord. With remembrance, they were performing a kind of austerity. At the time of the binding to the mortar, the Lord was three years old. For that many years they had His company. When the Lord is playing beside a person, pressed close, again and again, what a fortune that is. All this is the fruit of Narada's mercy. The nearness of Vasudeva. On the day of the binding, He uprooted both and delivered them. That was the last meeting. Before that, the company was there night and day.

12
00:43:40,770 --> 00:48:37,210
After that they will go to Alakapuri. In this universe there are very great cities. The most beautiful is Amaravati, Indra's capital. Alakapuri is of almost the same kind. Bhogavati is the city of the serpents. There is the city of Varuna. Such cities are not on this earth. They cannot even be imagined. Narada says, after remaining trees for so long, after receiving Krishna's nearness, after receiving devotion and love, then they will come to heaven and live there, filled with full Krishna consciousness. In heaven their katha will be another katha. The Lord sent them to heaven for that reason, after delivering them from the birth of trees. Narada is arranging it in this way. Then Shukadeva says, having spoken thus, the devarshi went to the ashram of Narayana. Nalakuvara and Manigriva became the twin arjuna trees. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10] Having said this much and given the curse, the sage of the demigods went to Narayana's ashram. Nara-Narayana, Badrikashram. They are the ones Narada worships. And these two brothers were born in Braj as trees. They became the yamalarjunas. Twins. Both spread equal branches. Height, breadth, everything alike. Having arranged their deliverance, Narada went to Narayana's ashram. Why? Sridhara Swami says Narada's wealth is austerity. Some austerity was spent in giving the curse, so let the austerity begin again, in Badrikashram. There was also a doubt in the mind. Was my work proper or not? Lord Narayana will say something with His own mouth. He went to hear it. The talk would certainly be there, that the demigod bodies of Kuvera's two sons were gone. It was a great event in heaven. In the Bhakti-rasayana, Sridhara Swami's feeling is that he went first to Narayana's ashram, so that one greater than himself, his own Lord, would confirm whether it was rightly done. However great a person is, when such a thing has happened he will want his Lord to confirm it. Sages gather there. Shankara goes. The four Kumaras go. The talk went on. The Lord said, you have shown great mercy. Then Narada's mind became completely at peace.

13
00:48:39,930 --> 00:52:02,310
To make true the word of the sage who is the best of the devotees, Hari went slowly to the place where the twin arjunas stood. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10] Mother Yashoda had bound Him in the courtyard. The courtyard had several parts. The two trees were in an outer courtyard. The Lord considered, Narada is dear to Me. Ahead it will come that Narada is My most dear limb, My devotee. He has said that these two will receive My mercy. Let Me give it to them quickly. But they should be taken out of the birth of trees and sent to heaven. Narada had said that after a hundred celestial years they would have Vasudeva's company, and after that they would go to heaven. The Lord considered that what Narada had said should be fulfilled. If He thinks of their deliverance, He first thinks that what Narada said is what must be done. What His dear one has said must be done. Devotees have this faith in the Lord. What we have said, the Lord will complete. An exclusive devotee has this kind of confidence. A shopkeeper was showing cloth, spreading it. The woman kept saying, I do not like it. The shopkeeper said, are you going to buy, or only to look? She was the wife of a very rich house. She felt hurt. She said, how much cloth is in your shop, what is the price of the whole shop, tell me, today I want to buy. The shopkeeper thought she was only talking. In fact she was ready. He said, I cannot sell the shop, but I am telling you all the cloth. She sent word to her husband. All the cloth in that shop was bought. How much faith that wife had. An exclusive devotee says, this should happen, and it will happen. The Lord will do it. Here He is thinking of the deliverance of Nalakuvara and Manigriva, and the first honor is that Narada has said it.

14
00:52:04,640 --> 00:55:16,020
Of the sages of the demigods, he is My dearest. My devarshi is the dearest of all. Once Srila Prabhupada was giving a class. He said, Prahlada Maharaj is the best of the devotees. Then he was asked. Sometimes you call Prahlada the best, sometimes Yudhishthira, sometimes Narada. Prabhupada said, yes, Prahlada is the best devotee of Krishna. Then Yudhishthira. He is the best of the best. Then the gopis. They are the best of those. Prabhupada did not call anyone less than the best. All are the best. Here the Lord is thinking, among the devarshis he is the dearest. There are many who are dear. When He speaks with Uddhava He says, Uddhava, as dear as you are to Me, My son Brahma is not that dear, and My own form, Shiva, is not that dear. In this way He honors the power of devotion. The devarshi is My dearest. And these are the sons of the giver of wealth. Sons of a very great man. Kuvera is My devotee. The world will say they have been delivered only when both are in their own forms, see the Lord, and speak with Him. Then they will say, yes, the deliverance has happened.

15
00:55:17,940 --> 00:57:41,920
I will accomplish what that great soul has declared. First He saw that Mother is absorbed in work. She will not stop Me. In the mood of a child's pastime, moving on His knees, with His hands, and pulling the mortar. He did not go standing up. He crawled. By the strength of His arms and by His knees. Slowly. So that the mortar would not strike the ground and make a sound. Mother would come and say, what are you doing, and she would tie it tighter. If she saw the mortar being dragged she would be astonished, and she could bind Him somewhere else. He was pulling very slowly, in an artful way. Before, without the mortar, He had passed those trees, in play. Today He passed, but the mortar was coming behind. It stuck. The Lord did not apply great force. Without manifesting opulence. As He moved, the mortar stuck and the rope went straight. He moved a little more. By then the roots of both trees tore out with a cracking. They fell with a crash. There was a very great sound. Like an explosion. It seemed a thunderbolt had fallen. Those who were working in the fields, those who were grazing cows, all ran. What has happened in the thunder, what calamity has happened.

16
00:57:42,140 --> 01:03:11,630
They began to look from a distance. The two arjuna trees could not be seen. They had been very tall. Some rakshasa has come and fallen. Earlier Trinavarta had come. Krishna had struck the cart with His small feet and turned it over. No one accepted that He had turned it. The children were saying, when He struck it with His foot the cart turned over. People began to scold them, be quiet. How can this child turn it over? The event had happened, and at that time too there had been a frightful sound. When Trinavarta fell, he roared very loudly. People began to guess. From the uprooting of the trees two celestial men were born. They appeared. Splendor like the sun. Narada's full favor. Birth in Braj. More beautiful than before. The children Mother Yashoda had appointed were watching, struck with wonder and speaking. Two demigods are praying to this child. One is kissing His feet. One is taking the dust of Braj and applying it. Nalakuvara and Manigriva are offering obeisances. The children were not greatly astonished. They were not afraid of the trees falling. They are absorbed in watching the pastime. When the cowherds sit in their assembly, how did the trees fall, someone will say he saw a terrible form, someone something else. The children will say, we saw nothing else. The mortar stuck, He pulled, and both trees were uprooted. He felled them. Then the scolding begins. What has happened to these children? Can trees fall because this child pulls? Even one who has the strength of ten thousand elephants could not uproot them. Will they fall because a child pulls? They will hear the talk of the cowherd men. Balarama will also come. He will be very displeased with Mother Yashoda. Why did you bind Him? The talk began. Some demon is felling things. Lord Narayana saved the child. Tomorrow he may fell something again. This place should be left. Until danger comes upon the child, we should leave this place. The cowherds had a very fine meeting. After that they left Gokula. Now they came to Vrindavan. Hare Krishna. This sitting is complete.

17
01:04:05,710 --> 01:08:44,780
He says it again. When Mother Yashoda had bound Him to the mortar and become absorbed in the housework, the Lord thought of delivering the two arjuna trees growing in that same courtyard. Of the sages of the demigods, he is My dearest. The devarshi is exceedingly dear to Me. So to obey the devarshi's word, to complete it, is My duty. I will certainly accomplish what that great soul has declared. He went between the two trees, dragging the mortar. How much space was there between them? Only enough for Himself to enter. The Lord was not very thick. A beautiful, well-adorned body. He got through. That was all the space. But the mortar went sideways. It was already moving sideways. Pulled by the child Damodara. In the next verse Shukadeva describes it. That child was pulling. It was stuck. He pulled. Seen with ordinary eyes, the feeling will be, who knows why it stuck. Which child applied the force? Damodara. The one who had a rope tied at the waist. Shukadeva is not saying that the Lord of unlimited opulence applied the force. By the child Damodara. The child who had the rope bound at His belly applied the force. In fact He did not pull the trees. He pulled the mortar. As soon as He pulled, with a jerk, the bonds of their feet were torn up. The feet of the trees, the roots, came out. Anghri means the foot. A tree's foot is its root, spread in the earth.

18
01:08:45,710 --> 01:14:39,900
They were very vast trees. Vast trunks, branches, and shoots. When Damodara gave the jerk they began to tremble very hard. Making a fierce sound. As trees are heard to fall, with that vast sound they fell forward. They fell with a great noise. Both fell toward Krishna, because Krishna was pulling that way. Even as they fell, the distance between them remained, so that Krishna would be saved between them. The Lord became bewildered. What has happened? That is how He was showing it. He was not showing, I am uprooting the trees, or I am delivering them. He is playing as a child. From the roots of the trees two perfected beings came out, illuminating all the directions. The word siddha is famous in the Bhagavatam. A class of demigods, or those who have become successful in every way. Their body, their language, everything is beyond nature. Siddhas move in heaven too, like the four Kumaras. Siddha means greatly effulgent. When life becomes perfect, a beautiful body is received. The splendor of Nalakuvara and Manigriva was such that the directions began to shine. They came out of the trees. Kuja means a tree. Ku means the earth, and ja means birth. One born from the earth. The astonishing thing: they came to the feet of that child bound to the mortar and offered obeisance with all eight limbs. They must have moved the trees a little to offer it, so that there would be room. They knew, this is not a child. This is the Supreme. But the Lord was still bound to the mortar. They bowed to Krishna with the head. Bowing the body, a full obeisance. The children standing around were astonished. What had happened on the bank of the Ganga? Why are these two bowing to this child? Shukadeva says, the Lord of all the worlds. They knew that Krishna is the Lord of all the worlds. The master even of Brahma, Shiva, and Indra. Akhila means the whole. The Lord of all living beings. Knowing this, they bowed. Both were viraja, free of passion. They were shining, clean, effulgent.

19
01:14:41,130 --> 01:17:40,680
Then, with joined hands, they began to speak. It is an astonishing moment. The Lord has been made dependent by Mother Yashoda. He is bound. And two perfected beings, freed beings, are praising Him. He is undergoing a punishment. Mother has bound Him by force. This is the Lord's astonishing image. These are the pastimes that draw the minds of the devotees very strongly. The Lord was smiling slowly. When they began the praise, the Lord began to laugh. The two brothers, with joined hands, say: Krishna, Krishna, O great yogi, You are the original person, the Supreme. The knowers of Brahman know this universe, manifest and unmanifest, to be Your form. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10] First, Krishna, Krishna. Srila Sanatana Goswami says the name Krishna is very dear, very sweet, so they said it twice. Twice means they must have said it many times. From the sweetness of the name. Or, He who attracts the mortar is Krishna. Karshati iti krishna. One who pulls is Krishna. Here their deliverance happened by that pulling. So the name dearest to them was Krishna.

20
01:17:43,570 --> 01:25:32,340
O great yogi. You are the original person, the Supreme. Those who herd cows and goats are not counted very intelligent by society's eye. The merchant and the ruler are counted intelligent. If a person stays all day with animals, what intelligence will develop? By the social eye they are counted low. The Lord became as if astonished. Why are you bowing to Me? Then they say, no, You are the great yogi. Yoga means unthinkable, unlimited opulence. You are possessed of unlimited and unthinkable opulence. Yoga also means the means that accomplishes the most difficult work. In the Lord there are unlimited energies. Creation of the universe, its maintenance, its destruction. Dwelling in every heart. The witness of all. If it is a matter of knowing place and time, in the eye of the human pastime a child would not even know whether the land of Hastinapura exists. In school a map is shown. But it is not that these energies are absent in the child from the beginning. What position today's child will attain later is not already in him. When he becomes very old, knowledge is destroyed. It is not so with the Lord. Whether He plays as a child, as Varaha, as Nrishimha, as Kapila, or as Sankarshana, at every time He is the complete Lord. He is speaking as if to say, how am I possessed of unthinkable opulence? Mother has bound Me so that I do not even have the opulence to get free. I am lying here dependent. They are saying, the opulence is unlimited. You are the source of the avataras, not an avatara. By the word purusha one should understand the Lord's original expansion, the purusha. The one who lies on the causal water. When scripture says purusha, generally that is meant. O Krishna, O You of unlimited opulence, You are not merely the purusha. You are the cause even of that purusha who dwells inside nature. You are beyond them. Therefore, the Supreme Person. The most excellent person. Three purushas are spoken of. Lying on the causal water, lying within the universe, lying in the heart of the living being. Remaining inside nature, they control maya. Whose portion of a portion is Govinda, the original person, Him I worship. Nalakuvara and Manigriva were very fortunate that they knew this secret. Adyah. You are the source of the avataras. The Supreme Lord is Krishna, the form of eternity, knowledge, and bliss. Govinda is without beginning and is the beginning, the cause of all causes. Govinda Himself has no beginning. He is the beginning of all. Therefore we are bowing. Today the binding is on that same Lord. Sridhara Swami says, bound by matra. Matra also means form, taste, and scent. And matra means Mother. The binding has been placed by Mother. We are in the binding of the material elements, and the Lord too has accepted the binding of Mother. The same Lord who impels the elements, nature, and everything. To tell His opulence, and to say this: the misbehavior we were doing in the Ganga, in the garden of Kailasa, of that too You are the cause. And of the words that came from Narada's mouth for our benefit, You are the mover.

21
01:25:59,000 --> 01:30:58,490
By Your mercy this became equal to worship. If there had not been such cities, we would not have received Your nearness. This does not mean that human beings should adopt this as their practice. What happened in the lives of Nalakuvara and Manigriva happened, in truth, by the Lord's will. The sight would not have come, but the Lord is the witness inside the heart. He controls everything. In spoken form Nalakuvara is saying, You are the Supreme Person, the controller of all, so You caused us to act in that way. Everything is in Your hand. We are grateful to You. Birth after birth we will remain in Your debt, that You showed such mercy. Sridhara Swami says it clearly: the mercy that came upon us is in truth Your mercy. They go so far as to say that, sitting in Narada's heart, You were merciful. The verse is like this. O Lord, the misbehavior we did, we did not do it. You caused it. And the words of the curse that came from Narada's mouth for us, he did not do that either. You did it. We take it as a favor done by You. This is the intention of the prayer. You are not only the instrument. Of this universe You are also the material cause. The knowers of Brahman know this manifest and unmanifest universe to be Your form. The brahmanas, the scholars who see through the Vedas, know that the manifest and unmanifest world, the gross and the subtle, is Your form. Form means that Your own energy has been transformed into the form of the universe. In this universe two kinds of things are experienced. Something very large, something very subtle. The large is called manifest, the small unmanifest. Or real and unreal, effect and cause. The words differ. Some things are not seen, so they are unmanifest. Mind, intelligence, ego. Air is not seen. The sky, in truth, is not seen. When the world becomes manifest, it has several causes. Form, taste, scent. From those the world is manifest. The meaning is that everything is made of Your energy. The soul is the doer of all and is present everywhere. It is a very beautiful prayer. Such things are said in hundreds of places in the Bhagavatam. The Lord is the cause of this world. This manifest and unmanifest universe is His form. Sometimes it can rise in the mind of a lover of the Bhagavatam, what is the need of repeating these things so often. This part ends there.
